I'm trying to think of a good way to allow people to easily access / set 
this info without spoiling people.  I'm thinking it pretty much has to 
be done through the web page, otherwise non-Windows users will be 
further disadvantaged.

Adding comments to each bones' web page can't be done anonymously, else 
it'd just be hit with comment spam.  So either users would have to log 
in to do it, or what they could add would have to be tightly restricted.  
One way of doing it would be to restrict them to posting a message ID to 
link to a rgrn YASD / YAAD which would explain it fully.

I suppose the simplest way of letting users know a bones-file comment is 
available for a bones file they've downloaded would be for the server to 
email them.

However, I can't tell when they've run into it except that once they 
leave bones on that level, I know they've either hit the bones file and 
died, or they've hit that bones file at some point in the past.  An 
alternative would be to wait a set amount of time after they hit a 
particular level before notifying them, but there is the risk there that 
they might be spoiled if the file is particularly deep in the dungeon, 
or just if they've taken a little break from hacking.

Hmmm...  still trying to think of a nice way to do this cleanly.

